: 'NumericIndicator.isLessThan(Number) - additional cases', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 'Long.MAX_VALUE'}], 'expected': 'Rule.isSatisfied(index) returns true for every index where the underlying NumericIndicator value is a finite number (i.e., all typical values), because no realistic value can be greater than or equal to Long.MAX_VALUE.', 'description': 'Very large positive constant (Long.MAX_VALUE) – verifies that the rule works correctly when the threshold is far beyond any possible indicator value.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 'Double.MIN_VALUE'}], 'expected': 'Rule.isSatisfied(index) returns true for indices whose value is negative or exactly zero, and false for any positive value ≥ Double.MIN_VALUE.', 'description': 'Smallest positive non‑zero double – tests the strict‑less‑than semantics around the zero boundary.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 'Float.valueOf(5.5f)'}], 'expected': 'Rule.isSatisfied(index) returns true when the underlying value < 5.5f, false otherwise.', 'description': 'Float constant – ensures that the method correctly handles Float Number implementations.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 'Short.valueOf((short)2)'}], 'expected': 'Rule.isSatisfied(index) returns true for values < 2 (as a short), false otherwise.', 'description': 'Short constant – verifies handling of smaller integral Number types.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 'Byte.valueOf((byte)-1)'}], 'expected': 'Rule.isSatisfied(index) returns true for values < -1, false for -1 and greater.', 'description': 'Byte constant – tests the method with the smallest integral wrapper type.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 'Double.NaN'}], 'expected': 'Rule.isSatisfied(index) always returns false (the rule never satisfies) because any comparison with NaN is defined as false.', 'description': 'NaN constant – checks that the rule fails fast for an undefined numeric threshold.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 'Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY'}], 'expected': 'Rule.isSatisfied(index) returns true for every finite underlying value (including negative, zero, and positive numbers), and false only when the underlying value is NaN.', 'description': 'Positive infinity – validates that the rule treats infinity as an upper bound that all finite numbers are less than.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 'Double.NEGATIVE_INFINITY'}], 'expected': 'Rule.isSatisfied(index) always returns false because no numeric value (including -Infinity itself) is less than negative infinity.', 'description': 'Negative infinity – ensures the rule never satisfies when the threshold is the lowest possible double.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 'new java.math.BigInteger("12345678901234567890")'}], 'expected': 'Rule.isSatisfied(index) returns true for underlying values < 12345678901234567890, false otherwise.', 'description': 'BigInteger constant – tests compatibility with another arbitrary‑precision Number subclass.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': '0.0'}], 'expected': 'Rule.isSatisfied(index) returns true when the underlying value is negative, false when it is zero or positive.', 'description': 'Zero as a Double – confirms that the method behaves identically for zero expressed as a floating‑point Number.'}]}]
